===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ped-}}
From {{der|en|enm|fetten}}, {{m|enm|feten}}, from {{der|en|ang|fetian}}, {{m|ang|fatian|t=to bring, fetch}}, probably a conflation of {{der|en|gem-pro|*fetaną|t=to go}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*ped-|t=to walk, stumble, fall}}; and {{der|en|gem-pro|*fatōną|t=to hold, seize}}, also from {{der|en|ine-pro|*ped-}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|vatten|t=to catch, grab}}, {{cog|de|fassen|t=to lay hold of, seize, take, hold}}. Compare also {{cog|is|feta|t=to find one's way}}. More at {{m|en|fetch}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb|fets|fetting|fet}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To [[fetch]].

